# Example .gitignore fragment — personal / local data stay out of git.
# HONEST LIMIT: ignoring paths is friction. A PR can delete these lines or
# widen the negation allowlist below; reviewers must treat .gitignore diffs
# that re-include personal paths as security-relevant.

# Default: keep personal and runtime state out
data/
logs/
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# Narrow negation allowlist — only reviewed, non-secret examples may be tracked.
# Adding a new ! exception belongs in the same PR as the file it unlocks.
!data/.gitkeep
!config/*.example
